				(size 3.048 3.048)
			)
		)
		(uuid "9dadcda3-6331-4253-8c62-2b2fa1588134")
	)
	(text "Current Sense Discussion\n\nFor this esc setup, the motor driver ensures that VREF/2 is the middle reference point for the current sensing, where here VREF is 3V3.\nFrom here, a gain of 10 is selected, in order to provide the mcu with an idle voltage of 1.65V when there is no current flowing through \na phase. This means, that under peak load (22A), we can expect a max voltage (assuming 4m shunt) of:\n\nV_out = 1.65 +- (Gain * I * R_shunt\n	  = 1.65 +-  (10 *  22 * 0.004) \n      = 2.53V\n\nThis is below the maximum of 3V3, which is ideal. This is because we need some headroom to detect if ever there \nis an overcurrent event in one of the phases. If this was too close, it would either have false detections, or be hard to detect\nsuch an event.\n\nWe can also calculate the maximum power dissipated trough this shunt as follows\n\nP = I^2 * R_shunt\n  = (22)^2 * 0.04 \n  = 1.94 W"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.986 242.062 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a1c33899-5dc3-46e2-96ef-adf4747b4556")
	)
	(text "This capacitor bank is expected to handle a total ripple current of:\ni_c = 0.65 * I_phase_rms * 1.1\n    = 0.65 * 15.56 *1.1 \n	= 11.12A\n\nThe total amount of capacitance required for full load would be:\nC = i_c /(delta_V * f_sw).\nGiven 10% max allowable voltage ripple on the DC Bus, capacitance required is:\nC = 11.12 / (2.4 * 25k)\n  = 185uF\n\nTaking a 15uF capacitor, we will need 12 caps, each capable of delivering 1A\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 83.058 68.834 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ac2aef24-abd5-438e-872b-7a4c35796673")
	)
